      "card_ids": ["C14", "C41", "C42", "C59"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "L3 oral exposure records for linezolid show substantial systemic exposure after oral dosing (AUCtau 82.8–99.2 µg·h/mL; median Cmax 18.3–18.9 µg/mL at 600 mg daily), consistent with high oral absorption.",
      "card_ids": ["C71", "C107", "C75", "C117"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "L4 Caco-2 permeability of linezolid was 21 × 10^-6 cm/s, and L5 rat ileum permeability was 24 × 10^-6 cm/s, indicating high intestinal permeability for the oxazolidinone scaffold.",
      "card_ids": ["C139", "C183"]
    }
  ],
  "new_evidence_assessment": [
    {
      "family": "gut_wall_efflux_intestinal_metabolism",
      "applicability": "moderate",
      "direction": "supportive",
      "decision_effect": "strengthened",
      "card_ids": ["C183"]
    }
  ],
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "Exact query molecule has no direct absolute oral bioavailability measurement.",
    "Query-specific Caco-2/rat permeability, efflux, solubility, and intestinal metabolism data are absent; L4/L5 permeability evidence is for linezolid, not the query.",
    "Structural differences from linezolid (5-chlorothiophene carboxamide replacing acetamide, morpholin-3-one replacing morpholine, no aryl fluorine) are not directly tested for absorption or first-pass effects.",
    "No experimental gut-wall efflux or intestinal metabolism data are available for the query."
  ],
  "decision_summary": "Predicted high and strengthened: linezolid, the closest oxazolidinone analog, has near-complete absolute oral bioavailability and high intestinal permeability in Caco-2 and rat ileum assays; L5 adds supportive gut-wall permeability evidence with no affirmative efflux/metabolism liability, and query physicochemical properties are favorable; no evidence supports F < 20%."
}

